Pennsylvania Dutch - Arc hum fem neu

This was a long slow struggle in early game. Got reasonably good armor
early on (+3 chain mail, CoP and +1 iron shoes), but had no BoH and
was constantly burdened. Switched to mithril, CoDisp and speed boots
when I had the chance, but AC went up to around -2. Found myself
messing around dlvl 15 or so with bad AC. Also had trouble finding ID
scrolls and a source of holy water. Only one altar on the main
dungeon, on dlvl 4, which I failed to convert on my first three tries
and gave up for a while. Finally converted later on in the game, and
sacrificing yielded first Cleaver and later Vorpal Blade. Twoweaponed
Vorpy with an elvish dagger for a while, waiting for a silver saber to
turn up, which it finally did, but not until down in Gehennom.

A relatively early unID'd amulet ended up being an amulet of change.
"You feel very feminine." I was always looking for another amulet of
change, but never came across one. I must have adjusted.

Meanwhile, I eventually got a BoH down around dlvl 19. Also ID'd ?oEA
and had one magic marker, so I got my AC down to about -30 eventually
(with the help of a throne wish for GDSM--wished for +3, got at +0).
Once I had non-metallic armor, I switched to a robe I'd stashed in
Minetown and began reading spellbooks. Soon got Magic Missile,
Fireball, and Cone of Cold to 0% fail.

I genocided L before doing the Castle, so it wasn't too tough.
Somehow, there was a dearth of musical instruments in the dungeon, so
even though I'd gotten the Passtune, I ended up going around the back
way to get into the Castle. Predictably, there was nothing of use in
the armory. I polypiled spellbooks and got as many spells as I could;
got to basic in attack, divination, and matter spells, which gave me a
lot of spells to use at 0% failure with my robe. Also poly'd some
unihorns to magic markers.

On the first level below the Valley, fell three levels through a trap
door and worked my way *up* through Juiblex's swamp and Asmodeus's
lair. Asmodeus summoned Baalzebub; beheaded both with Vorpal Blade;
later on, when I actually went through Baalzebub's lair, he wasn't
there, which was kind of a new one for me.

In the process of going up and down the dungeon to accomplish one goal
or another, right after restarting from a save, I killed a priestess
who didn't appear to belong to any temple (there were none outside the
guaranteed ones). I also robbed a grave once. I'm not sure if it was
one of those incidents or something else, but while looking for the
stairs to Vlad's, I recognized that I was at AC -21. It seems I'd lost
my protection! I wasn't sure how, so I just started gathering gold to
donate; however, when I donated to the priest in the Valley, I got the
"selfless generosity" message. Later, when saccing at my altar, I got
the "hopeful feeling" message (not the "feeling of unworthiness" one).
So my god didn't seem to be angry. I don't know how I lost protection,
but I abandoned the idea of getting it back and just enchanted my
armor up so I had AC -31 again, and went back down. Oddly enough, a
potion of enlightenment later told me I was protected, so I really
don't get what happened at all.

The main problem I had during the late game involved the fact that I
never had a late lucky ?oID identify all my stuff; in particular, the
charges on my wands. I finally felt ready to take on Rodney. Cone of
cold froze the moat, /oDig got me into the island, and then my /oDeath
missed Rodney. I got him on the second try, but that should have told
me something. The wand was cursed. (Another uncursed wand I had turned
out to be empty.) After getting the Amulet and working my way up
through Gehennom, Rodney appeared and I was out of charges. I
recharged the wand, but missed him several times before finally
finishing him off. He never double troubled me in this game, though,
and never stole anything; I ended up killing him five times.

In the Planes, I had the Orb of Detection confuse me twice rather than
reveal the portals; luckily, I also had some ?oGD to use as well.
Earth was easy (had /oDig collected from Gehennom), and then I ended
up using a lot of charges from my /oTels in Air (getting rid of
Elementals) and Fire (summoning storm trapped me among monsters for a
while); the result being that I didn't have enough charges while on
Astral. I actually had to take out a magic marker and a blank scroll
and write a scroll of charging while in the midst of melee in order to
break out of being surrounded.

I really didn't think I was going to survive Astral. The lack of a
really good weapon and being low on mana made the fighting a lot
harder than I recall with other characters. I had a lot of Archons
blinding me and I was stunned a lot; drank about 10 potions of full
healing to deal with Pestilence, whom I couldn't hit because of being
stunned and having my unihorn fail or just unblind me. Finally killed
him and got away; didn't encounter either of the other Riders. Guessed
wrong on the first two altars; offered the Amulet on the right one
with 110 hp (down from a max of 330 or so) and one !oFH left. After
ascending, I noticed in the text dump that I had a cursed luckstone; I
hadn't checked my inventory after malignant auras. So that was
probably part of my trouble as well.

This was to be my first YAAP using the Dump patch. However, my
8-year-old son decided to fire up a nethack game the morning after my
ascension. Of course, I hadn't copied my default dump file to another
file name, so the dump got overwritten. Most of the rest is from
memory or notes taken within the game.

